<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="8db0db56-dbb6-5d88-9fde-8ebc45ef6f40" activityNameId="87be823f-7966-5bf9-bca5-dd0c368790a9" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Underground mine, hard coal</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Underground mine, hard coal
Generic information for ecoinvent "underground mine, hard coal" GLO dataset was available only for a few mines. For the preparation of the GLO dataset only amounts per tonne were available. The dataset has to be considered as a first approximation and may not reflect specific (CN) mines. Lifetime is assumed to be 30 years to take into account the lifetime of machinery. The main mine shaft is assumed to be filled with concrete after the end of the lifetime, therefore the corrosion of the wood in the galleries is not accounted for. For defining the total production of a unit model mine, one million tonne per year has been estimated as an average worldwide (excluding small mines in China). This estimation includes open pit as well as underground mines. Therefore the total lifetime production of 30 million tonne shall be considered as a normalisation factor more than an actual average value for the real underground mines. Explosives are assumed to be used only during operation. In this CN dataset, electricity (total amount assumed for GLO) is arbitrarily assumed to be half from grid and half from local small coal power plants.;
UUID: 79bdba99-1510-328d-939e-243330d18882
This module includes an estimation of the most important construction materials and energy (electricity: CN) use for a model (GLO) mine. The landuse for the infrastructure is also included. The machinery used for mining operation has been included in this module, because the relevant material use is not separated from the total material use in the available references.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: No specific information available.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography/Text
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_79bdba99-1510-328d-939e-243330d18882.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
